<title>USA: Unisys seen making profit in '97 - report.</title>
<headline>Unisys seen making profit in '97 - report.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unisys Corp, should turn a profit in 1997 and has a &quot;bright&quot; long-term outlook, Business Week said.</p>
<p>An unnamed New York investment banker told Business Week he expects Unisys to post earnings of $0.50 a share in 1997, after an expected loss in 1996.</p>
<p>Officials at Unisys couldn't be reached for comment.</p>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's analyst Ted Groesbeck also told the magazine that Unisys' long-term outlook &quot;appears bright.&quot;</p>
<p>The mainframe maker's efforts to reduce operating costs and lower interest expenses will help Unisys return to profitability, Business Week said.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
